{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato","suddhaso"],"title":"6. The Astute","html":"<section class='range'  id='dhp76-89'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Khuddakanikāya </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Minor Collection </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Collection of Minor Texts </span></li>\n<li class='subdivision'><span class='root'>Dhammapada </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Sayings of the Dhamma 76–89 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Verses of Dhamma </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='range-title'><span class='root'>Paṇḍitavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>6. The Astute </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Chapter on the Wise </span></h1></header>\n<article id='dhp76'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Rādhattheravatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Nidhīnaṁva pavattāraṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Regard one who sees your faults </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Like a person who leads you to hidden treasure: </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>yaṁ passe vajjadassinaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>as a guide to a hidden treasure. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>this is how to see a person who points out your faults. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Niggayhavādiṁ medhāviṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stay close to one so intelligent and astute </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>A wise person who tells you what you need to subdue </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>tādisaṁ paṇḍitaṁ bhaje; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>who curbs you when you need it. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>is the kind of person you should associate with. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Tādisaṁ bhajamānassa, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Sticking close to such an impartial person, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Associating with that kind of person </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>seyyo hoti na pāpiyo. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>things get better, not worse. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>is always for the better and never for the worse. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp77'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Assajipunabbasukavatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Ovadeyyānusāseyya, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Advise and instruct; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>A person might advise you, instruct you, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>asabbhā ca nivāraye; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>curb wickedness: </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>and keep you away from what is not good; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Satañhi so piyo hoti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>for you shall be loved by the good, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>They are liked by those who are good, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>asataṁ hoti appiyo. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and disliked by the bad. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>and not liked by those who are not good. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp78'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Channattheravatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Na bhaje pāpake mitte, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Don’t mix with bad friends, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Do not associate with evil friends, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>na bhaje purisādhame; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>nor with the worst of men. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>do not associate with lowly people; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Bhajetha mitte kalyāṇe, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Mix with spiritual friends, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>associate with good spiritual friends </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>bhajetha purisuttame. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and with the best of men. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>and with the highest of people. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp79'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Mahākappinattheravatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Dhammapīti sukhaṁ seti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Through joy in the teaching you sleep at ease, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>When one enjoys the Dhamma, then one sleeps happily, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>vippasannena cetasā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>with clear and confident heart. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>with a clear mind; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Ariyappavedite dhamme, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>An astute person always delights in the teaching </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>a wise person always appreciates </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>sadā ramati paṇḍito. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>proclaimed by the Noble One. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>the Dhamma proclaimed by the noble ones. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp80'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Paṇḍitasāmaṇeravatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Udakañhi nayanti nettikā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>While irrigators guide water, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Irrigators guide water, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Usukārā namayanti tejanaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>fletchers bend arrows straight, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>fletchers shape arrows, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Dāruṁ namayanti tacchakā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>and carpenters bend timber straight, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>carpenters shape wood, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Attānaṁ damayanti paṇḍitā. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>the astute tame themselves. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>the wise train themselves. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp81'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Lakuṇḍakabhaddiyattheravatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Selo yathā ekaghano, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>As the wind cannot stir </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Just as the wind </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>vātena na samīrati; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>a solid mass of rock, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>does not move solid stone, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Evaṁ nindāpasaṁsāsu, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>so too blame and praise </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>praise and criticism </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>na samiñjanti paṇḍitā. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>do not affect the wise. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>do not disturb the wise. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp82'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Kāṇamātāvatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yathāpi rahado gambhīro, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Like a deep lake, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Like a deep lake, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>vippasanno anāvilo; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>clear and unclouded, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>clear and undisturbed, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Evaṁ dhammāni sutvāna, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>so clear are the astute </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>when the wise hear the Dhamma </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>vippasīdanti paṇḍitā. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>when they hear the teachings. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>they attain clarity. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp83'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Pañcasatabhikkhuvatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Sabbattha ve sappurisā cajanti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>True persons give up everything, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Good people let go of everything; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Na kāmakāmā lapayanti santo; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>they don’t cajole for the things they desire. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>the peaceful do not prattle about sensuality. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Sukhena phuṭṭhā atha vā dukhena, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Though touched by sadness or happiness, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Whether they are touched by pleasure or pain, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Na uccāvacaṁ paṇḍitā dassayanti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>the astute appear neither depressed nor elated. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>neither elation nor depression can be seen in the wise. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp84'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Dhammikattheravatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Na attahetu na parassa hetu, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Never wish for success by unjust means, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Whether because of oneself or because of another, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Na puttamicche na dhanaṁ na raṭṭhaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>for your own sake or that of another, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>one should not wish to obtain children, wealth, lordship, or personal success </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Na iccheyya adhammena samiddhimattano, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>desiring children, wealth, or nation; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>in ways contrary to Dhamma. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Sa sīlavā paññavā dhammiko siyā. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>rather, be virtuous, wise, and just. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Instead let one be virtuous, wise, and in accord with Dhamma. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp85'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Dhammassavanattheravatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Appakā te manussesu, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Few are those among humans </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Few are the humans </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>ye janā pāragāmino; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>who cross to the far shore. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>who go beyond. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Athāyaṁ itarā pajā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The rest just run around </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Most people </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>tīramevānudhāvati. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>on the near shore. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>only run around on the shore. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp86'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Ye ca kho sammadakkhāte, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>When the teaching is well explained, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Those who act in accordance </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>dhamme dhammānuvattino; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>the people who practice accordingly </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>with the well-explained Dhamma </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Te janā pāramessanti, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>will cross over </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>will go beyond the mortal realm </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>maccudheyyaṁ suduttaraṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Death’s dominion so hard to pass. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>so difficult to escape. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp87'><h2 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Pañcasataāgantukabhikkhuvatthu </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></h2>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Kaṇhaṁ dhammaṁ vippahāya, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Rid of dark qualities, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Abandon dark things and develop bright things; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Sukkaṁ bhāvetha paṇḍito; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>an astute person would develop the bright. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>a wise person </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Okā anokamāgamma, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Having left home for homelessness </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>leaves home for homelessness </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Viveke yattha dūramaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>in seclusion, where joy is hard, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>and lives in seclusion, where it is difficult to find satisfaction. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp88'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Tatrābhiratimiccheyya, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>they’d long for satisfaction there. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>One who has nothing could hope to find satisfaction there, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>hitvā kāme akiñcano; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Forsaking sensual pleasures, owning nothing, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>after abandoning sensuality; </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Pariyodapeyya attānaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>an astute person would cleanse themselves </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>a wise person would cleanse themselves </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>cittaklesehi paṇḍito. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>of mental corruptions. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>of mental defilements. </span></span></p></blockquote></article>\n<article id='dhp89'><blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yesaṁ sambodhiyaṅgesu, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>And those whose minds are rightly developed </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>Those who have developed the factors of awakening </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>sammā cittaṁ subhāvitaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>in the awakening factors; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>correctly and thoroughly, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Ādānapaṭinissagge, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>who, letting go of attachments, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>who have taken up relinquishment, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>anupādāya ye ratā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>delight in not grasping: </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>who appreciate non-grasping, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Khīṇāsavā jutimanto, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>with defilements ended, brilliant, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>and have eliminated their corruptions—</span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>te loke parinibbutā. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>they are quenched in this world. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'>such radiant beings have attained Nibbāna in this world. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endvagga'><span class='root'>Paṇḍitavaggo chaṭṭho. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='suddhaso'></span></p></article></section>"}
